WEBVTT

1
00:00:07.441 --> 00:00:10.477
Diego Alvarez: Morning, both. How's Austin treating you? Still stupid hot?

2
00:00:11.524 --> 00:00:19.054
Hector Ruiz: Man, it was 97 on Saturday. In October. My kid's soccer game, we we were all just melting on the sideline.

3
00:00:20.014 --> 00:00:28.562
Marisol Vega: And Phoenix is worse. My counterpart over there keeps sending me screenshots of his uh, car thermometer like it's a competition.

4
00:00:29.137 --> 00:00:40.137
Diego Alvarez: Um, Ha. Okay, so, what I wanted to do today is just a check-in. Volumes, anything on your end, and I know you flagged something on the agents.

5
00:00:40.137 --> 00:00:41.316
Diego Alvarez: How'd September land?

6
00:00:42.086 --> 00:00:55.047
Marisol Vega: September was strong. We did about 41,000 inbound across the three states, which is up maybe 12 percent over August. Google Ads is still carrying most of it, Meta's been softer since the middle of the month.

7
00:00:56.472 --> 00:01:04.971
Hector Ruiz: Softer is generous. The Meta leads, the quality just isn't there right now. But the Google side, yeah, we're getting good volume.

8
00:01:06.171 --> 00:01:15.419
Diego Alvarez: Got it. And the floor, are you fully staffed? I remember you were down a couple of Spanish reps in August.

9
00:01:16.532 --> 00:01:32.649
Hector Ruiz: We hired two. One started two weeks ago, the other's coming on the 19th. So we're almost there. The new guy, I've been sitting with him on calls, which is why I'm living in the QA tab lately.

10
00:01:33.269 --> 00:01:37.239
Diego Alvarez: Makes sense. Okay, tell me about the agents. What are you seeing?

11
00:01:38.180 --> 00:01:48.033
Hector Ruiz: So this is the thing I emailed you about. When the voice agent transfers to one of my reps, the context doesn't come through.

12
00:01:48.033 --> 00:01:55.013
Hector Ruiz: The rep picks up and the caller starts over. Name, address, what they want, all of it.

13
00:01:55.603 --> 00:02:03.985
Diego Alvarez: Okay. So the transfer itself happens, the call connects, but the rep doesn't get what the the agent collected.

14
00:02:04.799 --> 00:02:19.447
Hector Ruiz: Right. The note that's supposed to land with the call is empty. There's a note field, it's blank. So my rep is asking 'how can I help you' and the customer is like 'I already told the robot all this.'

15
00:02:20.444 --> 00:02:32.506
Marisol Vega: And it's not just annoying. On a solar call, if the customer already gave the address and and the utility and the roof type, and then they have to say it all again, we lose them.

16
00:02:32.506 --> 00:02:36.192
Marisol Vega: These are people who filled out a form forty seconds ago.

17
00:02:37.148 --> 00:02:48.032
Hector Ruiz: Last Tuesday I pulled, I don't know, eleven transfers, nine of them had the blank note. So it's most of them, not all of them.

18
00:02:48.856 --> 00:02:53.053
Diego Alvarez: So, okay, that's really helpful. When did you first notice it?

19
00:02:54.365 --> 00:03:04.365
Hector Ruiz: Maybe three weeks ago? It was around when we changed the the routing on the Spanish queue, but I honestly don't know if that's related.

20
00:03:05.648 --> 00:03:20.691
Diego Alvarez: Got it. Can you send me a couple of call IDs where it happened? Even two or three. I'll take it to the I mean, team and come back to you with what they find.

21
00:03:20.966 --> 00:03:26.785
Hector Ruiz: Yeah, I'll grab them after this. I've got them saved in a sheet already.

22
00:03:27.451 --> 00:03:31.849
Diego Alvarez: Perfect. Marisol, anything you you want to add on that?

23
00:03:32.741 --> 00:03:45.847
Marisol Vega: I'll add this. My boss asked me last week, point blank, whether we're renewing. And this handoff thing, the agent losing the context, that's the first thing I thought of.

24
00:03:45.847 --> 00:03:50.216
Marisol Vega: So I need to be able to tell him something.

25
00:03:50.940 --> 00:03:53.987
Diego Alvarez: When do you need to have that conversation?

26
00:03:55.359 --> 00:04:08.002
Marisol Vega: He wants a read by the end of the month. I'm not saying we're walking, but I can't go in there with 'it's being looked at.' I need a real answer.

27
00:04:08.687 --> 00:04:21.400
Diego Alvarez: Understood. I mean, Let me get the call IDs, get it in front of the right people, and I'll come back to you with a status, not a maybe.

28
00:04:21.400 --> 00:04:23.153
Diego Alvarez: Give me until Thursday.

29
00:04:24.467 --> 00:04:25.309
Marisol Vega: Thursday works.

30
00:04:26.572 --> 00:04:32.100
Diego Alvarez: Um, okay. Anything else on the tracking side, the Google Ads conversions, all that?

31
00:04:33.534 --> 00:04:35.755
Hector Ruiz: That's been fine. No complaints there.

32
00:04:36.520 --> 00:04:46.980
Diego Alvarez: Good. I'll send a calendar hold for Thursday, uh, say 11 your time, and Hector, just drop the call IDs in the thread whenever.

33
00:04:47.678 --> 00:04:49.110
Hector Ruiz: Will do. Thanks, Diego.

34
00:04:50.057 --> 00:04:54.733
Diego Alvarez: Thanks both. And Marisol, good luck with the soccer, so, Hector.

35
00:04:55.951 --> 00:04:57.587
Hector Ruiz: Ha, we lost. But thanks.
